11
00:50:46,153 --> 00:50:52,153
The film stars Richard Gere and Julia Roberts, and features Héctor Elizondo, Ralph Bellamy (in his
final performance), Laura San Giacomo, and Jason Alexander in supporting roles.

12
00:55:23,076 --> 00:55:29,076
The film's story centers on Hollywood escort Vivian Ward
and wealthy corporate raider Edward Lewis.

13
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Vivian is hired to be Edward's escort for several business and social functions,
and their relationship develops during her week-long stay with him.

14
01:04:36,923 --> 01:04:42,923
The film's title Pretty Woman is based on the 1964
song "Oh, Pretty Woman" by Roy Orbison.

15
01:09:13,846 --> 01:09:19,846
The original screenplay was titled 3000 and was
written by then-struggling screenwriter J.

16
01:13:50,769 --> 01:13:56,769
Originally intended to be a dark cautionary tale about class and prostitution in Los
Angeles, the film was reconceived as a romantic comedy with a large budget.

17
01:18:27,692 --> 01:18:33,692
Pretty Woman received mixed reviews from critics upon release, but widespread praise
was directed towards Roberts' performance and her chemistry with Gere.

18
01:23:04,615 --> 01:23:10,615
It had the highest number of ticket sales in the US ever for a romantic comedy, with Box Office Mojo listing it as the number-one romantic comedy by
the highest estimated domestic tickets sold at 42,176,400, slightly ahead of My Big Fat Greek Wedding (2002) at 41,419,500 tickets.

19
01:27:41,538 --> 01:27:47,538
The film grossed US$463.4 million worldwide and at the time of its release, was the
fifth-highest-grossing film of all time worldwide, behind only E.T.

20
01:32:18,461 --> 01:32:24,461
the Extra-Terrestrial ($701 million at the time), Star Wars ($530 million at the time), Indiana Jones
and the Last Crusade ($474 million at the time), and Jaws ($470 million at the time).

21
01:36:55,384 --> 01:37:01,384
It was also the highest-grossing R-rated film of all time (surpassing Rain Man) until it was surpassed by Terminator 2: Judgment Day in 1991, but remained the highest-grossing
R-rated film released by Walt Disney Studios, (surpassing Cocktail), holding the record for 34 years until Marvel Studios' Deadpool & Wolverine surpassed it in 2024.

22
01:41:32,307 --> 01:41:38,307
Pretty Woman catapulted Roberts to superstardom, earning her the Golden Globe Award for Best Actress – Motion Picture Comedy or Musical, in
addition to her first nominations for the Academy Award for Best Actress and the BAFTA Award for Best Actress in a Leading Role.

23
01:46:09,230 --> 01:46:15,230
The film also received nominations for the BAFTA Award for Best Film and the
Golden Globe Award for Best Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy.

24
01:50:46,153 --> 01:50:52,153
The film explores themes of prostitute, sports car,
capitalism, expensive restaurant, workaholic.

25
